---
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";

/**
 * The one page in this project that is not the instrument. It is static markup
 * with no island: the argument does not need a clock, and shipping React here
 * would mean the manifesto costs more to load than the app it describes.
 *
 * `/manifesto/`, not `/manifest/`: `/manifest.webmanifest` already exists and
 * means something else entirely.
 *
 * This does not break the one-route rule. That rule is about `/api/*` on the
 * Worker; a second static page is another file in `dist/`, served by the assets
 * binding, costing the product nothing.
 *
 * **It asserts. It does not explain, and it has no opponent.** The first draft
 * was six sections of how the software works; the second argued against list
 * calendars and against SaaS, which is positioning wearing a manifesto's
 * clothes. What is left is about time. No headings, because five headed
 * sections is a features page's skeleton. No `because`, no `which is`, no
 * `that is`: a joined-up argument invites disagreement with the joins, and
 * these are not arguments, they are statements. Three assertions stand alone
 * at size, plus the closer; if you add a fourth, delete one.
 */
---

<Base
  title="Manifesto · circal"
  description="Time does not run out in front of you. It comes back around. Why circal draws a day as one revolution."
  scroll
>
  <main class="mx-auto w-full max-w-[36rem] px-6 pt-14 pb-24 sm:pt-20">
    <a
      href="/"
      class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-ink-2 transition-colors hover:text-ink"
      aria-label="Open circal"
    >
      {/* The mark itself: black disc, one thin white circumference. */}
      <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="size-[15px]" aria-hidden="true">
        <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"
        ></circle>
      </svg>
      <span class="text-[15px] font-medium tracking-[-0.02em]">circal</span>
    </a>

    <h1
      class="mt-14 text-[34px] leading-[1.08] font-medium tracking-[-0.035em] text-balance text-ink sm:text-[44px]"
    >
      A day is a circle.
    </h1>

    {
      /* The borrowed line sits under the title rather than in a section of its
        own: it says the whole page in seven words, and it is credited at the
        foot. */
    }
    <p class="mt-5 text-[15px] leading-[1.5] text-ink-3 italic">You are a worm through time.</p>

    <p
      class="mt-10 text-[23px] leading-[1.35] font-medium tracking-[-0.02em] text-balance text-ink"
    >
      Time does not run out in front of you. It comes back around.
    </p>

    {
      /* Two up on a phone: at four across, a tile is 78px and the week's seven
        faces are 11px each, which is a smear rather than an argument. */
    }
    <figure class="mt-12 grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-8 gap-y-6 sm:grid-cols-4 sm:gap-3">
      <div>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" class="w-full" aria-hidden="true">
          <circle cx="32" cy="32" r="26" fill="none" class="stroke-ink-4" stroke-width="1.25"
          ></circle>
          <path
            d="M51.92 15.29A26 26 0 0 1 48.71 51.92"
            fill="none"
            class="stroke-accent"
            stroke-width="3"
            stroke-linecap="round"></path>
          <path
            d="M21.01 55.56A26 26 0 0 1 9.48 45"
            fill="none"
            class="stroke-ink-3"
            stroke-width="3"
            stroke-linecap="round"></path>
          <path
            d="M39.97 32.7 57.9 34.27"
            class="stroke-ink"
            stroke-width="1.25"
            stroke-linecap="round"></path>
        </svg>
        <figcaption class="label mt-2 text-center text-[10px] text-ink-3">Day</figcaption>
      </div>

      <div>
        {
          /* Seven faces at one rotation: the arcs sit at the same angle on
            every circle, which is the whole of what the week view says. The
            faces can only ever be a seventh of the tile wide, which is the
            strip's own constraint, so the strokes are the thinnest thing on
            the page: at 1.4 the arc was 40% of the radius and each face read
            as a filled blob rather than a face with something on it. */
        }
        <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" class="w-full" aria-hidden="true">
          {
            [4.57, 13.71, 22.86, 32.0, 41.14, 50.29, 59.43].map((cx) => (
              <g>
                <circle cx={cx} cy="32" r="4" fill="none" class="stroke-ink-4" stroke-width="0.6" />
                <path
                  d={`M${(cx + 3.06).toFixed(2)} 29.43A4 4 0 0 1 ${(cx + 3.98).toFixed(2)} 32.35`}
                  fill="none"
                  class="stroke-accent"
                  stroke-width="1.1"
                  stroke-linecap="round"
                />
              </g>
            ))
          }
        </svg>
        <figcaption class="label mt-2 text-center text-[10px] text-ink-3">Week</figcaption>
      </div>

      <div>
        {
          /* A dashed circle is a ring of marks for the price of one element;
             365 <line>s would be 20 KB of decoration. */
        }
        <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" class="w-full" aria-hidden="true">
          <circle
            cx="32"
            cy="32"
            r="25"
            fill="none"
            class="stroke-ink-3"
            stroke-width="6"
            stroke-dasharray="0.9 1.35"></circle>
          {
            /* A day carrying something is a *longer* mark, not a fatter one:
              `markRadius` grows outwards, so this matches the ring's own
              dash width and outreaches it. */
          }
          <path d="M48.47 18.18 55.75 12.07" class="stroke-accent" stroke-width="1.3"></path>
        </svg>
        <figcaption class="label mt-2 text-center text-[10px] text-ink-3">Year</figcaption>
      </div>

      <div>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 64 64" class="w-full" aria-hidden="true">
          <defs>
            <pattern id="m-lived" width="5.2" height="5.2" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
              <circle cx="1.3" cy="1.3" r="1.05" class="fill-ink-2"></circle>
            </pattern>
            <pattern id="m-left" width="5.2" height="5.2" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
              <circle cx="1.3" cy="1.3" r="1.05" class="fill-ink-4"></circle>
            </pattern>
          </defs>
          <rect x="5" y="8" width="54" height="22" fill="url(#m-lived)"></rect>
          <rect x="5" y="30" width="54" height="26" fill="url(#m-left)"></rect>
          <circle cx="27.1" cy="24.9" r="1.35" class="fill-accent"></circle>
        </svg>
        <figcaption class="label mt-2 text-center text-[10px] text-ink-3">Life</figcaption>
      </div>
    </figure>

    <p class="mt-6 text-center text-[13px] text-ink-3">The same shape, four distances.</p>

    <p class="mt-14 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-2">
      You were given twenty four hours today. You will be given twenty four tomorrow. There is no
      system, no arrangement and no amount of money that will get you twenty five.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-6 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-2">
      Every hour has one place on the face, and nothing you put there can also be somewhere else. A
      list hides that. A list takes everything you hand it and never once says the word full.
    </p>

    <p
      class="mt-10 text-[23px] leading-[1.35] font-medium tracking-[-0.02em] text-balance text-ink"
    >
      A circle says it immediately.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-10 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-2">
      You will do this about twenty nine thousand times. They fit on one screen, the first to the
      last, and you are somewhere in the middle of it as you read this.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-6 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-2">
      Nothing on that screen says whether a day was worth having. It counts. It does not grade.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-6 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-2">
      Nobody is keeping these for you. No account, no server, no copy on anyone else's machine.
    </p>

    <p
      class="mt-10 text-[23px] leading-[1.35] font-medium tracking-[-0.02em] text-balance text-ink"
    >
      Which means you are keeping them.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-10 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-2">
      The return is not a punishment. It is the offer. Tomorrow the rim goes dark, the face comes up
      empty, and the whole of it is handed back.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-6 text-[17px] leading-[1.75] text-ink-2">
      Fill it on purpose. Leave it empty on purpose. Both are decisions. Drifting is not.
    </p>

    <p
      class="mt-14 text-[27px] leading-[1.25] font-medium tracking-[-0.025em] text-balance text-ink"
    >
      The circle closes so that it can open.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-16 border-t border-hairline pt-8">
      <a
        href="/"
        class="inline-flex h-9 items-center rounded-[9px] bg-ink px-4 text-[13.5px] font-medium text-void transition-opacity hover:opacity-90"
      >
        Open circal
      </a>
      <p class="caption mt-6 text-ink-3">
        “You are a worm through time” is the opening line of the Hiss incantation, from Control
        (Remedy Entertainment, 2019).
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
